  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nThe table shows the production of different types of household items (in lakhs) by a certain company over the years.\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nAnnual growth rate for an item from year Y₁ to year Y₂ is given by:\n\n {Growth Rate} = frac{{Production in Y}₂ - {Production in Y}₁}{{Production in Y}₁} times 100 \n\n**Calculation:**\n\nCalculating growth rates:\n\nFor Item P:\n\n2017: (72 - 70)/(70) times 100 = (2)/(70) times 100 = 2.86\\% \n\n2018: (75 - 72)/(72) times 100 = (3)/(72) times 100 = 4.17\\% \n\n2019: (80 - 75)/(75) times 100 = (5)/(75) times 100 = 6.67\\% \n\n2020: (85 - 80)/(80) times 100 = (5)/(80) times 100 = 6.25\\% \n\n2021: (88 - 85)/(85) times 100 = (3)/(85) times 100 = 3.53\\% \n\nFor Item Q:\n\n2017: (90 - 80)/(80) times 100 = (10)/(80) times 100 = 12.5\\% \n\n2018: (95 - 90)/(90) times 100 = (5)/(90) times 100 = 5.56\\% \n\n2019: (100 - 95)/(95) times 100 = (5)/(95) times 100 = 5.26\\% \n\n2020: (90 - 100)/(100) times 100 = (-10)/(100) times 100 = -10\\% \n\n2021: (110 - 90)/(90) times 100 = (20)/(90) times 100 = 22.22\\% \n\nFor Item R:\n\n2017: (70 - 75)/(75) times 100 = (-5)/(75) times 100 = -6.67\\% \n\n2018: (80 - 70)/(70) times 100 = (10)/(70) times 100 = 14.29\\% \n\n2019: (90 - 80)/(80) times 100 = (10)/(80) times 100 = 12.5\\% \n\n2020: (95 - 90)/(90) times 100 = (5)/(90) times 100 = 5.56\\% \n\n2021: (100 - 95)/(95) times 100 = (5)/(95) times 100 = 5.26\\% \n\nFor Item S:\n\n2017: (100 - 90)/(90) times 100 = (10)/(90) times 100 = 11.11\\% \n\n2018: (100 - 100)/(100) times 100 = (0)/(100) times 100 = 0\\% \n\n2019: (110 - 100)/(100) times 100 = (10)/(100) times 100 = 10\\% \n\n2020: (118 - 110)/(110) times 100 = (8)/(110) times 100 = 7.27\\% \n\n2021: (120 - 118)/(118) times 100 = (2)/(118) times 100 = 1.69\\% \n\nFor Item T:\n\n2017: (52 - 50)/(50) times 100 = (2)/(50) times 100 = 4\\% \n\n2018: (58 - 52)/(52) times 100 = (6)/(52) times 100 = 11.54\\% \n\n2019: (60 - 58)/(58) times 100 = (2)/(58) times 100 = 3.45\\% \n\n2020: (64 - 60)/(60) times 100 = (4)/(60) times 100 = 6.67\\% \n\n2021: (70 - 64)/(64) times 100 = (6)/(64) times 100 = 9.38\\% \n\nFor Item U:\n\n2017: (85 - 80)/(80) times 100 = (5)/(80) times 100 = 6.25\\% \n\n2018: (90 - 85)/(85) times 100 = (5)/(85) times 100 = 5.88\\% \n\n2019: (110 - 90)/(90) times 100 = (20)/(90) times 100 = 22.22\\% \n\n2020: (120 - 110)/(110) times 100 = (10)/(110) times 100 = 9.09\\% \n\n2021: (148 - 120)/(120) times 100 = (28)/(120) times 100 = 23.33\\% \n\n**∴ The correct answer is option 4, Items R in 2018 with a growth rate of 14.29%.**",
